React me Context API ek built-in feature hai jo data ko parent component se deeply
nested child components tak props pass kiye bina share karne ke liye use hota hai.

ContextAPI se ap data ko centralized kar dete hai,
Ek jagah data rakho aur jahan zaroorat ho wahan use kar lo.

Sab components usi ek source se data le rahe hain.

           UserContext
                |
      --------------------
      |        |        |
   Navbar   Profile  Dashboard

Yehi centralized state management kehlata hai.

Interview Answer

"Context API data ko centralized is tarah karti hai ke hum shared state ko Provider
me ek jagah store kar dete hain aur useContext hook ke through application
ke kisi bhi child component me access kar sakte hain, 
jis se props drilling avoid hoti hai aur state management easy ho jata hai."

Problem (Props Drilling)

Agar data App se Child3 tak bhejna ho:

<App>
  <Child1>
    <Child2>
      <Child3 />
    </Child2>
  </Child1>
</App>

<App user="Farhan" />

Phir Child1, Child2, aur Child3 sab me props pass karne padenge. Isko props drilling kehte hain.

Solution: Context API

Context API se data directly kisi bhi component me access kar sakte hain

Step1: Context create karo

// UserContext.js

import { createContext } from "react";

const UserContext = createContext();

export default UserContext;

Step2: Provider lagao

// App.jsx

import UserContext from "./UserContext";
import Home from "./Home";

function App() {
  const user = "Farhan Ahmed";

  return (
    <UserContext.Provider value={user}>
      <Home />
    </UserContext.Provider>
  );
}

export default App;

value me jo data doge wo sab child components access kar sakte hain.

Step3: Data use karo

// Profile.jsx

import { useContext } from "react";
import UserContext from "./UserContext";

function Profile() {
  const user = useContext(UserContext);

  return (
    <h1>Welcome {user}</h1>
  );
}

export default Profile;

Interview Definition

Context API React ka built-in state management system hai jo components ke darmiyan data share karne ke liye use hota hai aur props drilling ko avoid karta hai.

Yaad rakhne ka simple formula:

React Context API ke important interview questions aur short answers:

1. Context API kya hai?

React ka built-in feature jo data ko multiple components me share karne ke liye use hota hai bina props drilling ke.

2. Props Drilling kya hoti hai?

Jab parent component ka data intermediate components ke through pass karna pade sirf child tak pahunchane ke liye.

App → Child1 → Child2 → Child3
3. Context API ke main parts kya hain?
createContext()
Provider
useContext()
4. createContext() ka kya kaam hai?

Context object create karta hai.

const UserContext = createContext();
5. Provider kya hota hai?

Data provide karta hai jitne bhi child components us context ko use karna chahte hain.

<UserContext.Provider value={user}>
  <App />
</UserContext.Provider>
6. useContext() kya karta hai?

Context ke data ko consume (receive) karta hai.

const user = useContext(UserContext);
7. Context API aur Props me kya difference hai?
Props	Context API
Parent → Child data	Global-like data sharing
Props drilling hoti hai	Props drilling avoid hoti hai
Simple cases ke liye	Shared data ke liye
8. Kya Context API Redux ko replace kar sakta hai?

Small aur medium projects me haan.

Large applications me Redux, Zustand ya Redux Toolkit zyada suitable hote hain.

9. Kya multiple contexts bana sakte hain?

Ji haan.

const UserContext = createContext();
const ThemeContext = createContext();
10. Context API ki limitations kya hain?
Frequent updates par unnecessary re-renders ho sakte hain.
Complex state management ke liye ideal nahi.
Redux Toolkit ya Zustand zyada scalable hote hain.
11. useContext hook kis React version me introduce hua?

React 16.8 me Hooks ke sath.

12. Default value createContext me kaise dete hain?
const UserContext = createContext("Guest");

Agar Provider na mile to "Guest" return hoga.

13. Context API kab use nahi karni chahiye?

Jab data sirf parent aur direct child ke beech share ho raha ho.

<Parent>
  <Child />
</Parent>

Is case me props hi best hain.

14. Context API me object pass kar sakte hain?

Bilkul.

<UserContext.Provider
  value={{
    name: "Farhan",
    age: 22
  }}
>
15. Context API ka sabse common use case kya hai?
Authentication
Theme (Dark/Light Mode)
Language Switching
User Data
Cart Data
